  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This large-leaved deeply divided cultivar has greenish leaves which are pink flushed in the spring, becoming greenish bronzed with pink dots and blotched variegation. However, like many maple variegates, the richer the growing conditions, the less the variegation until it disappears altogether. A curious feature of 'Wakehurst Pink' is that, sometimes, on fully developed leaves, the outer lobes are deeply divided to within 5 mm of the leaf base whereas, with the central lobe, the lobe junctions are 1. 5-2 cm from the leaf base. The large-lobed leaves are 8. 5-9. 5 cm long and 10. 5- 12 cm wide. They are long-ovate with tail-like pointed tips, and regular sharp-pointed hooked teeth around the margins. The basal lobes tend to spread at right angles to the petioles. The purple-red petioles are 3-4. 5 cm long with swollen bases. The upright growth habit is similar to that of"
  },
